The domain boundary also needs an explicit contract: decide where tokens become trusted principals and whether purchase and preview require the same authorization policy, then make both paths follow it. Similarly, `route` currently sends every kind other than `'purchase'` to preview; whether unknown kinds must be rejected is unresolved without the route policy. These observations do not establish deployed defects. The active build binding, production cache lifetime and remaining tests are also unknown.

